WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:03.460
- I am a true California girl.

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:04.330
I am.

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:06.830
I love it here for so many reasons,

00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:10.110
but mostly because this is a place

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.860
that is a year round destination

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:14.980
with so many amazing outdoor events.

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:18.260
We actually teamed up
with Visit California

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:21.720
to drop in on an event the other night.

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:22.623
Take a look.

00:00:24.069 --> 00:00:26.510
We are about to crash a movie screening.

00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:28.640
That's right, because in California,

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:30.980
the weather is so beautiful that you can

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:33.340
sit under the twinkling stars

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:35.170
and the gorgeous city lights,

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:38.220
and actually watch a movie outside.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:40.560
But what you don't know is that the movie

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:41.840
is actually 50 First Dates.

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:43.550
So I'm gonna go and surprise some people.

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:44.793
Let's see how this goes.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.103
Hi everybody.

00:00:48.336 --> 00:00:50.405
(crowd applauds)

00:00:50.405 --> 00:00:53.810
Hi!

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:56.410
My name is Drew Barrymore,

00:00:56.410 --> 00:01:00.400
and I wanted to come and personally

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:02.890
present this movie to you tonight.

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:05.580
It just seemed like a
wonderful opportunity

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:10.270
on this gorgeous California
night in this warm weather,

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:13.490
to be able to enjoy a movie that is

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:16.970
happy and joyful and hopeful.

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:18.870
And ironically really talks about

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:21.240
the challenges we face in life.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:23.320
I think this is why I've always wanted

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:27.160
to make films like a 50 First Dates.

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:29.750
So it's a pleasure to have gotten to do

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:33.080
movies that I think do
put you in a good mood.

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:36.860
And you know, if anyone has
a question about the movie,

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:40.750
I was there and I could answer
any fun trivia or facts.

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:42.360
I see a hand raised,

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:43.680
- Hi Drew.

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:44.690
- Hello.

00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:46.120
- I've been a big fan my whole life.

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:48.100
So thank you for your work and

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:50.253
all that you've done
for making us happier.

00:01:51.587 --> 00:01:52.420
- Thank you.

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:53.253
- I really appreciate it.

00:01:53.253 --> 00:01:56.030
I guess I was wondering,
in context of this movie,

00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:58.070
if there's ever been a day in your life

00:01:58.070 --> 00:02:00.980
that you wanted to relive
over and over again.

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:03.350
- Oh my gosh, that's such a good question.

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:04.520
- [Woman] Thank you.

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:07.350
- It would definitely be
a day with my daughters.

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:11.490
Until I met them, life was
just, you know, fun and dandy.

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:14.650
But when I met them,
like everything changed.

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:17.740
So any day where the
three of us are there,

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:20.870
is the day I want to stay in permanently.

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:23.260
Thank you for asking me that question.

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:25.170
I saw you raised your hand.

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:26.003
- Hi.

00:02:26.003 --> 00:02:27.213
I love you.

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:28.046
I love your show.

00:02:28.046 --> 00:02:28.879
- I love you.

00:02:28.879 --> 00:02:29.950
- I literally just got
here from Toronto today,

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:31.620
so this is a really interesting surprise.

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:32.930
- Welcome to California.

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:34.400
- Thank you.

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:37.180
So I know that you film
your show in New York,

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:40.170
so what's the reason that you're here?

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:42.450
- So one of the things
that we wanted to do

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:44.230
with season two of the show,

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:47.290
because season one, we weren't
able to travel anywhere,

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:49.530
and I always saw this show as something

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:51.770
we would take on the road.

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:52.970
I'm from California.

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:55.500
I now live in New York and
it's a really fun chapter,

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:58.260
we're not gonna lie,
but these are my roots.

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:02.340
I love California and nights like this,

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:05.270
and to see a skyline and greenery

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:07.840
is something that I miss so much.

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:10.860
There really is no place like California.

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:13.610
It's weird that you can be
at an ocean, a mountain,

00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:17.160
a desert, and a forest
all within 30 minutes.

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:19.980
This is a very magical state.

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:24.410
So I just felt like kicking
the season two off here.

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:25.780
Do you want to ask one last question?

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:27.700
I see a raised hand right there.

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:30.730
- Thank you for taking the
time to answer some questions.

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:33.850
My mom came too, she's in town.

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:35.580
We are huge fans of yours.

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:38.220
Ever After is our all-time favorite movie,

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:39.980
as well as Never Been Kissed.

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:41.810
So I just wanted to know if you ever

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:45.630
had a favorite movie that
you enjoyed working on.

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:49.070
- You just named the two movies
that really changed my life,

00:03:49.070 --> 00:03:50.443
and Charlie's Angels too.

00:03:52.043 --> 00:03:53.700
(crowd applauds)

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:56.520
When it comes to filmmaking,

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:59.470
I wanted feelings at
the end of these films

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:02.300
and for Ever After, I
wanted people to feel like,

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:04.830
I am in control of my own destiny.

00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:06.940
I wanted for 50 First Dates for people

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:08.530
to have faith and believe in

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:10.890
the goodness of people and love,

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:13.240
and Charlie's Angels, yeah,

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:15.190
I wanted to drive a stick shift

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:18.480
and get into fourth gear, maybe fifth.

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:21.080
But tonight I hope you let

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:23.590
everything fall away for a moment

00:04:23.590 --> 00:04:27.020
and watch something that, I promise you,

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:30.510
we all made for you to feel good.

00:04:30.510 --> 00:04:34.570
So thank you for letting me
invade your space tonight,

00:04:34.570 --> 00:04:36.270
and may you have such a beautiful,

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:38.182
wonderful rest of your evening.

00:04:38.182 --> 00:04:39.015
Thank you.

00:04:39.015 --> 00:04:40.821
(crowd applauding)

00:04:40.821 --> 00:04:41.830
- [Woman] We love you.

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:44.390
- I love you more.

00:04:47.977 --> 00:04:49.420
(crowd applauding)

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:51.610
That was so much fun.

00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:53.800
I really do love surprising people.

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:55.290
I love when people do it to me

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:57.090
and I've actually totally gotten,

00:04:57.090 --> 00:04:58.950
gotten into doing it to people.

00:04:58.950 --> 00:05:01.050
So that was really fun,

00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:06.050
and you kind of never
know what you're gonna get

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:09.080
during a night out in California.

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:11.160
You might even bump into me.

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:12.672
I'm just saying.

00:05:12.672 --> 00:05:15.172
(theme music)

